# deploy/fasrc-dev/scripts/host.env.example — per-host overrides for lib.sh.
#
# Copy to host.env in this same directory. host.env is git-excluded
# (.gitignore rule: deploy/fasrc-dev/scripts/**/*.env); this example IS tracked.
# lib.sh sources host.env BEFORE it applies its defaults, so a host pins its own
# deployment identity without editing a tracked file.
#
# Write overrides with the `: "${VAR:=value}"` form. That form sets the value
# only when the variable is not already set, so a one-off on the command line
# still wins:
#     DEPLOYMENT=elsewhere ./redeploy.sh
# A plain VAR=value assignment instead OVERRIDES the command line — that
# behavior is pinned by test_host_env.sh (case 6). Use the := form unless you
# really mean that.
#
# Reserved names (issue #363):
#   dev   — the GPU host (holygpu7c0717 / archi.rc.fas.harvard.edu), the only
#           production deployment. It needs no host.env: with no file, lib.sh
#           resolves exactly the tracked defaults.
#   claw  — the no-GPU / no-local-vLLM developer workstation.

# --- GPU host (holygpu7c0717) — no host.env needed; shown for completeness ---
# : "${DEPLOYMENT:=dev}"
# GPU_IDS stays at the tracked default (empty): both containers are configured
# `device: cpu`, and on this host the GPUs are owned by the vLLM servers.

# --- no-GPU workstation -------------------------------------------------------
# : "${DEPLOYMENT:=claw}"
# : "${CONFIG:=deploy/fasrc-dev/config.yaml}"   # per-host config (git-excluded)
